distinct critical points. If no source lies on <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, the same
bound holds with analytic multiplicity.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Use (<a href="#S7.E73" title="Equation 73 ‣ 7. Point-charge consequences ‣ Critical Points of Line Restrictions of Signed Point-Charge Potentials" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) and put <math id="S7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=p/2&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=p/2&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Positive
coefficients prevent class cancellation, though duplicate restricted
kernels may combine, so the effective count satisfies <math id="S7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the smooth case, write <math id="S7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}(u,v)=c_{i}(u-a_{i}v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}(u,v)=c_{i}(u-a_{i}v)</annotation></semantics></math>. The corresponding
projective section also satisfies</span></p>
