<p id="S7.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">so it has no zero at infinity.
The applicable alternative of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Reduced signed Maxwell-line dichotomy). ‣ 2. Reduction and main results ‣ Critical Points of Line Restrictions of Signed Point-Charge Potentials" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a> gives at most
<math id="S7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2m-1\leq 2n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2m-1\leq 2n-1</annotation></semantics></math> critical points. If all sources are off the line, every
effective height is positive and the smooth multiplicity statement applies.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 7.2</span></span><span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(EFO Conjecture 3)<span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For positive charges written in the EFO form <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}=\zeta_{i}^{p}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}=\zeta_{i}^{p}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the
substitution <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=2\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=2\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> identifies their line derivative with the
positive specialization of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Reduced signed Maxwell-line dichotomy). ‣ 2. Reduction and main results ‣ Critical Points of Line Restrictions of Signed Point-Charge Potentials" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.
Consequently, Conjecture 3 of Edelsbrunner–Fillmore–Oliveira holds throughout its stated range
<math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>; moreover, the same conclusion holds for every <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the planar Gabrielov–Novikov–Shapiro (GNS) restriction to the <math id="S7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-axis, the parameters
are <math id="S7.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}^{2}=y_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}^{2}=y_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus terms <math id="S7.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> define the same restricted
kernel precisely when <math id="S7.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},y_{i}^{2})=(x_{j},y_{j}^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},y_{i}^{2})=(x_{j},y_{j}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 7.3</span></span><span id="S7.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Natural reduced GNS formulation)<span id="S7.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the signed setting of GNS Conjecture 1.9, combine equal restricted
kernels and delete zero class sums. Exact cancellation occurs precisely
when every class sum is zero. Otherwise, if <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> effective classes
remain, there are at most <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2m-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2m-1</annotation></semantics></math> regular critical points with the smooth
and singular counting conventions of <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Reduced signed Maxwell-line dichotomy). ‣ 2. Reduction and main results ‣ Critical Points of Line Restrictions of Signed Point-Charge Potentials" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.
Thus, outside the exact-cancellation case, the reduced GNS bound
holds throughout the GNS range <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and in fact for every <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The word <em id="S7.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">line</em> is essential in both corollaries. Neither statement
asserts the unrestricted multidimensional Maxwell conjecture.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8. </span>Examples and positive optimality</h2>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following examples display cancellation, mixed signs, a zero total
coefficient, and a source on the line before we establish the positive
extremal construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 8.1</span></span><span id="S8.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Reflected exact cancellation)<span id="S8.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Restrict to the <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-axis and take sites <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, with
coefficients <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Both sites induce the pair
<math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b^{2})=(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b^{2})=(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, so their class sum is zero and</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}(t)=\frac{1}{(t^{2}+1)^{\alpha}}-\frac{1}{(t^{2}+1)^{\alpha}}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}(t)=\frac{1}{(t^{2}+1)^{\alpha}}-\frac{1}{(t^{2}+1)^{\alpha}}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for every <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here <math id="S8.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and every ordinary point is
critical. This is the literal exception that necessitates the reduced GNS
formulation.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 8.2</span></span><span id="S8.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(A nonzero mixed-sign restriction)<span id="S8.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">At <math id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math>, consider</span></p>
<table id="S8.E78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(78)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(t)=\frac{2}{t^{2}+1}-\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(t)=\frac{2}{t^{2}+1}-\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Its two kernels are distinct, so <math id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="S8.E79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(79)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\prime}(t)=\frac{-2P(t)}{(t^{2}+1)^{2}(t^{2}-4t+5)^{2}},\qquad P(t)=t^{5}-14t^{4}+50t^{3}-76t^{2}+49t+2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>14</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>76</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>49</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\prime}(t)=\frac{-2P(t)}{(t^{2}+1)^{2}(t^{2}-4t+5)^{2}},\qquad P(t)=t^{5}-14t^{4}+50t^{3}-76t^{2}+49t+2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The exact values are</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(P(-1),P(0),P(2),P(3),P(9),P(10)\bigr)=(-188,2,4,-76,-2068,2892)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>188</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>76</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2068</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2892</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(P(-1),P(0),P(2),P(3),P(9),P(10)\bigr)=(-188,2,4,-76,-2068,2892).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">These sign changes give a zero of <math id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in each of
<math id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1,0)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,3)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S8.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(9,10)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(9,10)</annotation></semantics></math>. The smooth paired bound is three
counted with multiplicity. Hence these are exactly the three real critical
points, one in each displayed bracket, and all are simple.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 8.3</span></span><span id="S8.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Zero total coefficient and an infinity zero)<span id="S8.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Still at <math id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math>, take</span></p>
<table id="S8.E80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(80)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(t)=\frac{1}{t^{2}+1}-\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(t)=\frac{1}{t^{2}+1}-\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The total coefficient is zero, but the two kernels are distinct and
<math id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=2</annotation></semantics></math>. Direct calculation gives</span></p>
<table id="S8.E81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(81)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F^{\prime}(t)=\frac{4\bigl(3(t-1)^{4}-4\bigr)}{(t^{2}+1)^{2}(t^{2}-4t+5)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F^{\prime}(t)=\frac{4\bigl(3(t-1)^{4}-4\bigr)}{(t^{2}+1)^{2}(t^{2}-4t+5)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Thus the two finite real critical points are</span></p>
<table id="S8.E82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(82)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1\pm\left(\frac{4}{3}\right)^{1/4}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1\pm\left(\frac{4}{3}\right)^{1/4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and both are simple.
For the paired section <math id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E=-F^{\prime}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>F</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=-F^{\prime}/2</annotation></semantics></math>, the representative in the complementary
projective chart is <math id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\infty}(s)=s^{-3}E(1/s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\infty}(s)=s^{-3}E(1/s)</annotation></semantics></math>, which
extends analytically to <math id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=0</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfies <math id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\infty}(s)=-6s+O(s^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\infty}(s)=-6s+O(s^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
It therefore has a simple infinity zero:
the zeroth numerator sum vanishes, while the next coefficient does not.
Thus the two finite roots together with the infinity zero have total
projective multiplicity three, exactly the <math id="S8.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2m-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2m-1</annotation></semantics></math> budget.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 8.4</span></span><span id="S8.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(One effective source on the line)<span id="S8.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S8.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}(t)=|t|^{-2\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}(t)=|t|^{-2\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, the reduced domain is
<math id="S8.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="S8.E83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(83)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{\alpha}^{\prime}(t)=-2\alpha\operatorname{sgn}(t)|t|^{-2\alpha-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sgn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{\alpha}^{\prime}(t)=-2\alpha\operatorname{sgn}(t)|t|^{-2\alpha-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There is no critical point in either component. The pole <math id="S8.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> is
outside the domain and is not critical;
Remark <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem4" title="Remark 6.4 (Refined singular bound). ‣ 6.3. One global count in the singular case ‣ 6. Proof of the signed line theorem ‣ Critical Points of Line Restrictions of Signed Point-Charge Potentials" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.4</span></a> gives the sharp bound <math id="S8.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2m-r-1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2m-r-1=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The next result concerns positive configurations only. It proves that
the <math id="S8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n-1</annotation></semantics></math> bound in terms of the original number <math id="S8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> of charges cannot be lowered uniformly; it
does not assert a separate signed optimality theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 8.5</span></span><span id="S8.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Positive universal sharpness)<span id="S8.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, take the line to be the <math id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-axis and
place unit positive charges at</span></p>
<table id="S8.E84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(84)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{i}=\left(i,\frac{1}{4n},0\right),\qquad i=1,\ldots,n." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}=\left(i,\frac{1}{4n},0\right),\qquad i=1,\ldots,n.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The restriction of <math id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> to the line has exactly <math id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n-1</annotation></semantics></math> distinct
critical points, all simple. Consequently</span></p>
<table id="S8.E85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(85)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\#\operatorname{Eq}(V_{p}|_{\Lambda})=2n-1\qquad(p&gt;0)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>#</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Eq</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\#\operatorname{Eq}(V_{p}|_{\Lambda})=2n-1\qquad(p&gt;0),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the maximum ranges over positive <math id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-charge configurations and
straight lines.
Here, <math id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Eq}(V_{p}|_{\Lambda})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Eq</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Eq}(V_{p}|_{\Lambda})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of critical points of <math id="S8.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{p}|_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p}|_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> in its regular domain.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Put</span></p>
<table id="S8.E86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(86)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E86.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="a_{i}=i,\qquad b=\frac{1}{4n},\qquad c_{i}=1,\qquad i=1,\ldots,n," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=i,\qquad b=\frac{1}{4n},\qquad c_{i}=1,\qquad i=1,\ldots,n,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">and define</span></p>
<table id="S8.E87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(87)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{p,n}(t)=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{t-j}{\bigl((t-j)^{2}+b^{2}\bigr)^{1+p/2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{p,n}(t)=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\frac{t-j}{\bigl((t-j)^{2}+b^{2}\bigr)^{1+p/2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Along the <math id="S8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-axis, <math id="S8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{p}^{\prime}=-pE_{p,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p}^{\prime}=-pE_{p,n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume first that <math id="S8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. At <math id="S8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=i\pm b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>±</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=i\pm b</annotation></semantics></math>, the self term has
magnitude</span></p>
<table id="S8.E88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(88)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{p,n}=2^{-1-p/2}(4n)^{p+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{p,n}=2^{-1-p/2}(4n)^{p+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S8.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq i</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|t-j|\geq 1-b\geq\frac{3}{4}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|t-j|\geq 1-b\geq\frac{3}{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">and, with <math id="S8.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1+p/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1+p/2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S8.E89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(89)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{|t-j|}{\bigl((t-j)^{2}+b^{2}\bigr)^{\beta}}&lt;|t-j|^{1-2\beta}\leq\left(\frac{4}{3}\right)^{p+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{|t-j|}{\bigl((t-j)^{2}+b^{2}\bigr)^{\beta}}&lt;|t-j|^{1-2\beta}\leq\left(\frac{4}{3}\right)^{p+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">The self term dominates the sum of the remaining terms because</span></p>
<table id="S8.E90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(90)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{S_{p,n}}{(n-1)(4/3)^{p+1}}=\frac{3n}{2(n-1)}\left(\frac{3n}{\sqrt{2}}\right)^{p}&gt;\frac{3}{2}&gt;1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{S_{p,n}}{(n-1)(4/3)^{p+1}}=\frac{3n}{2(n-1)}\left(\frac{3n}{\sqrt{2}}\right)^{p}&gt;\frac{3}{2}&gt;1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="S8.E91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(91)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.E91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{p,n}(i-b)&lt;0&lt;E_{p,n}(i+b)\qquad(i=1,\ldots,n)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{p,n}(i-b)&lt;0&lt;E_{p,n}(i+b)\qquad(i=1,\ldots,n).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S8.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2b=1/(2n)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2b=1/(2n)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="S8.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n</annotation></semantics></math> test points are ordered as</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-b&lt;1+b&lt;2-b&lt;2+b&lt;\cdots&lt;n-b&lt;n+b." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-b&lt;1+b&lt;2-b&lt;2+b&lt;\cdots&lt;n-b&lt;n+b.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">Their signs alternate. The intermediate value theorem supplies a zero in
each of the <math id="S8.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n-1</annotation></semantics></math> disjoint intervals between consecutive test points.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The smooth paired Haar theorem bounds the sum of the multiplicities of all
zeros by <math id="S8.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n-1</annotation></semantics></math>. We have already found that many distinct zeros, each of
multiplicity at least one. Hence there are exactly <math id="S8.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n-1</annotation></semantics></math> zeros, and
each is simple. When <math id="S8.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1</annotation></semantics></math>, the unique zero is <math id="S8.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{p,1}^{\prime}(1)=b^{-2-p}&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{p,1}^{\prime}(1)=b^{-2-p}&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">so it is simple as well.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The results concern <math id="S8.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. At <math id="S8.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S8.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant on its regular domain, and no assertion is made about the limit <math id="S8.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
